      "seed": 1588783452,
      "version": 201,
      "versionNonce": 1391150995,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791489168128,
      "created": 1791293262154,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "ii) litralarls ->  is instance of a primitive type \n\n        ex -> 4 -> number litral\n            -> \"hell0\" -> string litral\n            -> true -> boolean litral ",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "ii) litralarls ->  is instance of a primitive type \n\n        ex -> 4 -> number litral\n            -> \"hell0\" -> string litral\n            -> true -> boolean litral ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "DfFtN6DtSSRTp2R9HRGsW",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1472.0775285799673,
      "y": 1161.803177793681,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 105,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "az",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1659749732,
      "version": 204,
      "versionNonce": 1138941235,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791489168128,
      "created": 1791293510312,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "ex -> const direction = \"east\" | \"west\" | \"north\" | \"south\"\n\nso direction = string litral = only can have value / those 4",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "ex -> const direction = \"east\" | \"west\" | \"north\" | \"south\"\n\nso direction = string litral = only can have value / those 4",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "bWo0R9iLJRt3-cC4u_lNX",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1504.4557237645595,
      "y": 1317.302971170668,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 560,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b03",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 174305764,
      "version": 699,
      "versionNonce": 144096979,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791489168128,
      "created": 1791293960210,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "iii) enums -> enables u to maintain a collection of fixed\nconst like litrals \n             \n            -> with each value linked to a rep no \n         const in enum -> to number (not the other way)\n            means -> small, mid, large \n                            -> can't get 0 -> small\n                            -> can get small -> 0\n        \n            -> syntax -> enum name{collection_of_const}\n\n       -> can manually map ur no's to enum's each guy too\n            if u don't want default 0,1,2...\n\n      -> above ones we used are doing numeric rep against \n            my individual enum",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "iii) enums -> enables u to maintain a collection of fixed const like litrals \n             \n            -> with each value linked to a rep no \n         const in enum -> to number (not the other way)\n            means -> small, mid, large \n                            -> can't get 0 -> small\n                            -> can get small -> 0\n        \n            -> syntax -> enum name{collection_of_const}\n\n       -> can manually map ur no's to enum's each guy too\n            if u don't want default 0,1,2...\n\n      -> above ones we used are doing numeric rep against    \n            my individual enum",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "d9lQ-mf_9JqtJ7Dgjjom_",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1517.9832503435132,
      "y": 1909.6854479682909,
      "width": 785.232177734375,
      "height": 210,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b09",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1117359411,
      "version": 229,
      "versionNonce": 2073914483,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791489168128,
      "created": 1791484215152,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "iv) enums types -> numeric and string enums\n\n        syntax of string enum ->  enum enum_name{\n                                                use = \"freeuse ok\"\n                                                    }\n                    en_name.use gives now -> freeuse ok",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "iv) enums types -> numeric and string enums\n\n        syntax of string enum ->  enum enum_name{\n                                                use = \"freeuse ok\"\n                                                    }\n                    en_name.use gives now -> freeuse ok",
      "autoResize": true,
